    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d580">

                <pb facs="0736" n="728" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg728"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.458/34: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to the Shah of Iran</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Reza Shah Pahlavi</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-03-13">March 13, 1938</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>It affords me great pleasure to extend to Your Majesty cordial birthday greetings
                    and my sincere best wishes for a long, happy and prosperous reign.</p>
                <p>With the near approach of the Iranian New Year festivities, I likewise wish to
                    express the hope that the coming year will witness the strengthening of those
                    close bonds of friendship which for so long have united the American and Iranian
                    peoples.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Franklin D.
                    Roosevelt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
